 picture='The separate picture measures answer support on twelve fixed questions from one approved collection. A supports nine answers, or 75%; B supports ten, or approximately 83.333%. The difference is one supported answer, about 8.333 percentage points. This is a support outcome, not evidence that any learner became smarter. No user learning, timings, significance or stable population effect is supplied. Keep the main eight-versus-nine pass case separate from this nine-versus-ten support case. A broader question about learners would require its own appropriate design and evidence, not a stronger adjective in the conclusion.',
